# Build context for the Quartz Dockerfile. The image copies the checkout with
# `COPY . .`, so keep local installs, build output, and npm configuration out
# of the context. Dependencies are installed inside the image.
#
# `.git` stays in the context on purpose: quartz.config.ts asks
# CreatedModifiedDate to read page dates from git history before falling back
# to filesystem timestamps, and without the repository every undated page
# would carry the image's build time instead.
.github
node_modules
public
.quartz-cache
.npmrc
.env
.env.*
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
